          model: "The quality and quantity of the food we eat affect both our brains and our bodies. Healthy foods such as fruit, vegetables, fish and nuts give the brain the energy it needs to think and remember. They also help the immune system fight germs and keep our muscles and bones strong. On the other hand, unhealthy foods like fast food and sweets can make us tired and overweight. Too much salt raises blood pressure and increases the risk of heart disease and stroke. I wish more people knew this. If we chose our food carefully, we would live healthier lives.",
